---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import Plate from '../components/Plate.astro';
import { THREE_WORDS } from '../lib/site';

const commitments = [
  {
    title: 'We accept compensation from no one but our client.',
    body: 'No referral fees, finder’s fees, rebates or commissions from builders, subcontractors, suppliers, designers, manufacturers or lenders. Not disclosed-and-accepted. None.',
  },
  {
    title: 'We hold no interest in any construction company.',
    body: 'We don’t build, own a builder, or take equity in one.',
  },
  {
    title: 'You sign the construction contract.',
    body: 'Directly, with your licensed general contractor. We never contract for construction work — a deliberate structure that in some jurisdictions is also what makes the independence lawful.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The specialists we retain are paid by us, on your behalf.',
    body: 'Engineer, cost consultant, inspectors. None of them have a relationship with your contractor.',
  },
  {
    title: 'We recommend firms we would use ourselves, and we say why.',
    body: 'Including when the answer is a firm we have no relationship with.',
  },
  {
    title: 'We will tell you when you don’t need us.',
    body: 'Some projects don’t. Saying so costs a fee and earns a referral.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Everything discussed is confidential by default.',
    body: 'No client name, project or image is published without written permission. Many of our clients would prefer not to be named anywhere, and that is the normal case rather than the exception.',
  },
];
---

<Article
  title="Independence — Whose Side We’re On"
  heading="Whose side we’re on"
  kicker="The standing commitment"
  description="No referral fees from builders. No interest in any contractor. You sign the construction contract. Our independence commitment in full."
>
  <p>The entire proposition rests on one thing, so it should be written down and dated.</p>

  <div class="not-prose mt-10 border-y border-rule">
    <dl class="grid gap-8 py-8 md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        THREE_WORDS.map((item) => (
          <div class="border-l border-rule pl-5">
            <dt class="font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-accent">
              {item.word}
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 max-w-xs text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">{item.line}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>

  <p class="not-prose annotation mt-8">The seven commitments behind those three words:</p>

  <div class="not-prose mt-4">
    <ol class="max-w-prose">
      {
        commitments.map((c, i) => (
          <li class="grid grid-cols-[3rem_1fr] border-t border-rule py-6">
            <p class="annotation pt-1">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">{c.title}</h2>
              <p class="mt-2 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink/90">{c.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>

  <Plate
    src="/plates/plate-08-scaffold.svg"
    alt="Repeating grid of scaffolding standards, ledgers and diagonal braces"
    caption="Independence is structure, not sentiment."
    class="my-12 aspect-[16/9]"
  />

  <h2>One of us came from the industry</h2>
  <p>
    Geordie spent five years inside a prefabricated housing company, latterly as Vice President and Partner.
    That is where a good deal of the knowledge comes from, and it is a fair thing to ask about.
  </p>
  <p>
    The answer: we take no compensation from any manufacturer or builder, that one included, and we don’t
    steer clients toward or away from any company. Understanding exactly how these businesses price, schedule
    and allocate risk — from the inside — is precisely what makes the representation worth paying for.
    Someone who has never sat on that side of the table cannot tell you which parts of a contract have room
    in them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Who we are, in full, is on <a href="/who-we-are">the team page</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="not-prose mt-12 border-t border-rule pt-8 max-w-prose text-base font-medium">
    If any of these commitments stops being true, this page changes first.
  </p>
  <p class="annotation not-prose mt-3">Committed August 2026.</p>
</Article>
